# The move stick: the speed at five tilts straight ahead, the direction at stick angles between the axes at full
# and at 0.4 tilt, the player's Walking button held at full tilt, and the stick after that button's release. Every
# sample starts at one spot of DmDeck16 with 1,100 units free along yaw 32768, its view turned so that the stick's
# direction runs along that yaw:
#   tools/dev/inputtest/run.sh <run-tree> move.scen <out-dir> 'DmDeck16.unr?Game=UnrealI.DeathMatchGame' \
#       -SOFTWARERENDERER '-ini:System:[UnrealI.DeathMatchGame]:InitialBots=0'
#   tools/dev/inputtest/rate.py <out-dir>/game.log 0
# The tags name the tilt and the stick's angle in degrees clockwise from straight ahead (speed-0.4: 0.4 ahead;
# dir-0.4-30: 0.4 at 30 degrees, which rate.py's "move" should read as 30). The pad's Y button is Joy4, the Walking
# button of the shipped layout.
waitlog DmDeck16.*up for play
sleep 3
pad attach
sleep 1
pad axis righttrigger 32767
sleep 0.3
pad axis righttrigger 0
sleep 3
exec TELEPORT 1045 -1472 -724 32768
sleep 0.3
pad axis lefty -6553
sleep 2.4
watch 20 speed-0.2
sleep 1.2
pad axis lefty 0
sleep 0.8
exec TELEPORT 1045 -1472 -724 32768
sleep 0.3
pad axis lefty -13107
sleep 2.4
watch 20 speed-0.4
sleep 1.2
pad axis lefty 0
sleep 0.8
exec TELEPORT 1045 -1472 -724 32768
sleep 0.3
pad axis lefty -19660
sleep 2.4
watch 20 speed-0.6
sleep 1.2
pad axis lefty 0
sleep 0.8
exec TELEPORT 1045 -1472 -724 32768
sleep 0.3
pad axis lefty -26214
sleep 2.4
watch 20 speed-0.8
sleep 1.2
pad axis lefty 0
sleep 0.8
exec TELEPORT 1045 -1472 -724 32768
sleep 0.3
pad axis lefty -32767
sleep 2.4
watch 20 speed-1.0
sleep 1.2
pad axis lefty 0
sleep 0.8
exec TELEPORT 1045 -1472 -724 30948
sleep 0.3
pad axis leftx 5690
pad axis lefty -32269
sleep 1.2
watch 20 dir-1.0-10
sleep 1.2
pad axis leftx 0
pad axis lefty 0
sleep 0.8
exec TELEPORT 1045 -1472 -724 27307
sleep 0.3
